Recommends:
 iptables,
 systemd-resolved,
Description: NetworkManager VPN plugin that tunnels with sshuttle
 nm-sshuttle runs sshuttle as a NetworkManager VPN connection. The tunnel is
 brought up, supervised and torn down by a small root service. ssh runs as the
 logged-in user, so the user's keys, agent and ~/.ssh/config apply.
 .
 The design needs systemd-resolved for per-link DNS; without it the DNS
 settings of a profile degrade to "every lookup goes to the VPN's servers".

Package: nm-sshuttle-gnome
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 network-manager (>= 1.42),
 nm-sshuttle (= ${source:Version}),
Description: GNOME Settings editor for nm-sshuttle profiles
 Adds "sshuttle" to the VPN types that GNOME Settings can add and edit, so
 that a profile can be made and changed there instead of with
 `nm-sshuttle add`. The editor is a GTK4 library that GNOME Settings loads;
 it has no GTK3 counterpart for nm-connection-editor yet.
 .
 Without this package GNOME Settings still lists and switches the profiles,
 but cannot edit them.
